About

I architect systems that bridge the gap between complex theory and real-world impact. As a Computer Engineering student at SIT Lonavala, I am on a mission to master the convergence of Web3, AI, and Quantum Computing to solve scalable problems. My journey is defined by a "builder's mindset"—taking concepts from the whiteboard to deployment. 

🏆 Defining Achievement: Smart India Hackathon (SIH) 2025 Winner Leading my team, "Algo Sapiens," we secured victory at the SIH 2025. Our project, "Telhan Sathi," not only addressed critical agricultural challenges but made history as the first-ever entry from SIT Lonavala to reach the national finals. This victory reinforced my ability to lead high-performance teams under pressure.

🛠️ Technical Innovation & Research I document my innovations. I engineered a "Collaborative Code Editor" for distributed teams and published a research paper on its architecture in the International Research Journal of Modernization in Engineering Technology and Science (IRJMETS). My portfolio also includes "CityConnect," a civic engagement platform built with Next.js, Django, and a custom JS Blockchain. Currently, I am exploring Quantum Algorithms (Qiskit) and DeSci to revolutionize verifiable research.

👨‍💼 Leadership & Community As the Head of Cybersecurity and Blockchain for the Institution's Innovation Council (IIC) at SIT, I bridge security principles with blockchain transparency. I also organize major events like "Project Morpheus 2026" (hackathon) and "Kalpataru" (robotics bootcamp). Recently, I served as a mentor for the "CODE2LAUNCH" workshop, teaching web fundamentals to junior developers.

📚 The Grind Consistency is key. I am deep into rigorously preparing for GATE 2026 with a comprehensive study schedule covering 14+ engineering subjects.

I am looking to connect with visionaries in Web3, Quantum, or Deep Tech. Let’s build something that matters.

